    "number": 249,
    "title": "Refresh the work guide to current GitHub status",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nRefresh the cross-project work guide to current GitHub state before public publication.\n\n- **Snapshot.** Backlog read at 2026-09-24 23:20 UTC: 118 open issues (Hub 66, Nanoleaf 33, Pixoo 19). Merged-work history read at 23:20 UTC from Hub `28f7599`, Nanoleaf `9e2c413` and Pixoo `0ca009c`.\n- **Coverage.** Removes 8 issues that closed since the last edition: Hub #231; Nanoleaf #78, #108, and #10 to #14 (the Lively wallpaper track, closed as not planned under Nanoleaf #134). Assigns the 32 new open issues a primary guide:\n  - Monitoring accuracy: Hub #241, Nanoleaf #110.\n  - B.U.N.N.Y. controls: Hub #247.\n  - Nanoleaf wall map: Nanoleaf #111, #112, #115, #117, #135.\n  - Adding devices (Panels): Nanoleaf #113, #114.\n  - Pixoo media: Pixoo #79.\n  - Music: Hub #242.\n  - Hosting: Nanoleaf #131, #132.\n  - Engineering maintenance: Hub #240, #244, #245, #246; Nanoleaf #118 to #124, #127 to #130; Pixoo #80, #81, #82.\n- **Engineering maintenance tracks.** That guide grows to 20 issues, so it now splits into Hub, Nanoleaf and Pixoo tracks, as Adding devices already does. The generator now fails if a track list leaves out a guide row. Before this change, an untracked row disappeared without an error.\n- **Stale prose.** Rewrites the next steps, Useful next steps, decisions and reading notes that still described closed work as pending (one-step settings, thread links, default layout, Lively). Adds archive rows for Hub #231 and #237 and for Nanoleaf #108, #78, #133 and the Lively closure (#134).\n- **Roadmap.** Retires the Lively node. Adds tracks for session retirement, change notifications, Panels controller access, task metadata, comets, and Hub, Nanoleaf and Pixoo code maintenance. Adds cross edges for Nanoleaf #121's recorded start condition (after #111, #112 and #115). The three tracks that `reconcile()` appended now live in `TRACKS`, so cross edges and the dependency test can reference them.\n- **Checks.** Swaps examples that pointed at issues now closed or changed: Nanoleaf #10 becomes #114; the blocker-injection test uses Hub #232 and now also checks that it is a next step before the injection; the Hub #218 search phrase is updated.\n- **Diagrams.** No change. The architecture views and the atlas are untouched.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py` passed at head `73f5e615b85466741148cbe532779d01b378aac3`. Rebuilding after commit produced no output drift. Guide SHA-256: `63409762044b57c77a9f6edefd1c3c42e4da45a97ac176a5a25a571c4cbbcece`.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py` passed (12 tests).\n- `node docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs` passed (Node 24.21.0, Playwright 1.63.0, Chromium 1243). It covers navigation, search, task briefs, live and offline status, the timeline, diagrams and print restoration at desktop and phone widths. The two console errors it logs are its own simulated 429 and aborted requests, the same as the previous edition.\n- I inspected the roadmap, the Engineering maintenance, Nanoleaf wall map, monitoring and hosting guides, and the opening lists at 1440 and 390 px.\n- `git diff --check` passed. All 23 changed paths are under `docs/work-guide/`.\n- Screenshots, the print PDF and the verification log are kept outside Git in the main checkout at `.local/evidence/guide-publish-20260924b/`.\n\n## UI approval and guide-only CI\n\n- **Affected UI:** the generated guide only (topic guides, opening lists, roadmap, archive). All of it is under `docs/work-guide/`, so the [guide UI exemption](https://github.com/jimmie-potts/agent-device-hub/blob/main/docs/sdlc.md#ui-approval-scope) applies. No viewer, atlas or application UI changes.\n- **Guide-only CI exception:** the receipt follows as a PR comment after reviews.\n\n## Known gaps (owner follow-ups)\n\n- Nanoleaf #120 and #121, and still #16, #19 and #20, carry `blocked` labels whose prerequisites appear only in their bodies. The guide therefore shows \"Reconcile the issue body\" for them. This PR adds no native blocked-by links; that tracker write needs the owner's go-ahead.\n- A2 (system map) and the BUNNY atlas still carry evidence notes from their earlier pin, as the previous edition recorded.\n\nThis is a dated snapshot. It installs nothing and operates no devices. The public publication PR follows after reviews, merge and the guide-only CI receipt.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
